3. FFmpeg                                               LGPL v2.1 or later
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Statically linked into app/src/main/jniLibs/*/libffmpegJNI.so, when a build has
one. Not present in the source tree, and not required to build Choir.

    Copyright (C) 2000-2023 the FFmpeg developers
    https://ffmpeg.org/

Built from the unmodified upstream release tagged in tools/build-ffmpeg.sh,
configured with --disable-everything and an explicit decoder list, which
excludes every component FFmpeg licenses under the GPL. The result is therefore
LGPL v2.1-or-later, which the GNU GPL v3 permits incorporating.

The corresponding source is the tagged upstream release, and tools/build-ffmpeg.sh
fetches exactly it and reproduces this binary from it. Choir itself is under the
GPL v3, so the relinking freedom the LGPL requires is already granted by the
application's own licence — the whole application is source-available and
modifiable.


